hifiberry-sendspin (0.1.6) trixie; urgency=medium

  * postinst: do not restart config-server. When the web interface installs
    an extension, config-server is the process running apt and it holds the
    install job the UI polls in memory, so restarting from the postinst --
    which runs during dpkg's configure step, mid-install -- destroyed that
    job. The package installed correctly (apt runs under systemd-run and
    survives) but the UI reported the install as lost. The restart was also
    unnecessary: configurator re-reads conf.d in place after every extension
    install.

 -- HiFiBerry <support@hifiberry.com>  Thu, 20 Aug 2026 18:30:00 +0000

hifiberry-sendspin (0.1.5) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Player descriptor: declare a maintainer at all. The descriptor carried
    no maintainer_name, so the card showed nothing where every other player
    shows either a name or a call for one -- silence that read as though
    the question had never been asked rather than as unmaintained. Now
    Wanted, so it reads "Looking for maintainer".

 -- HiFiBerry <support@hifiberry.com>  Thu, 20 Aug 2026 14:00:00 +0000

hifiberry-sendspin (0.1.4) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Extension icon: use sendspin's own icon, now carried by
    hifiberry-webui 0.21.9 so it resolves before the extension is
    installed. The generic stand-ins were both wrong: music.svg rendered
    too thin (115-unit viewBox against the set's 23) and
    music-note-simple-light.svg too heavy (a fill-designed silhouette
    stroked with fill:none traces the outline of the outline).

 -- HiFiBerry <support@hifiberry.com>  Thu, 20 Aug 2026 12:15:00 +0000

hifiberry-sendspin (0.1.3) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Extension icon: use music-note-simple-light.svg instead of music.svg.
    music.svg is drawn on a 115-unit viewBox where every other icon uses
    23, so at the same stroke-width its lines came out five times thinner
    and rendered as a pale grey smudge next to the other extension cards.

 -- HiFiBerry <support@hifiberry.com>  Thu, 20 Aug 2026 12:00:00 +0000

